# Repository-owned line-ending policy.
#
# Generated artifact instances and the deterministic fixture subjects they are
# produced from are written by tooling with LF endings. Without a rule the
# worktree representation depends on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting,
# so a Windows checkout followed by regeneration reports every generated file as
# modified when nothing about its content changed.
#
# This governs repository representation only. The canonical serialization of an
# artifact is the JSON Canonicalization Scheme (STD-0010 R-46) and the content
# digest is computed over that serialization (STD-0008 R-55); neither is a
# property of how a file is stored in a worktree.
#
# text=auto rather than text: a file whose content Git detects as binary is left
# untouched, so a future binary fixture is not corrupted by normalization.

artifacts/** text=auto eol=lf
fixtures/** text=auto eol=lf
